<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec unemployment rate unchanged at 3.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec unemployment rate unchanged at 3.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate in December remained unchanged from November at 3.3 percent, while the closely watched jobs-to-applicants ratio rose to 0.76 in December from 0.74 the previous month, the government announced on Friday.</p>
<p>It also said the average unemployment rate for 1996 edged up to 3.4 percent, compared to 3.2 percent the previous year, reaching the highest level since 1953, the earliest date for which comparative figures are available.</p>
<p>The jobs-to-applicants ratio rose to 0.70 in 1996 from 0.63 in 1995.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			   December  November  Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.3 pct   3.3 pct   3.4 pct</p>
<p>					 December  November  year ago</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio	 0.76	0.74	0.64</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)			 December  November  Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.1 pct   3.2 pct   3.2 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	     2.08 million  2.12 million  2.11 million</p>
<p> Number of employed		 December    Year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				64.55 million	+0.9 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p> Manufacturing			14.37 million	-0.1 pct</p>
<p> Services			     15.97 million	+1.7 pct</p>
<p> Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.71 million	+0.2 pct</p>
<p> Construction			  6.92 million	+3.4 pct</p>
<p> Agriculture			   2.70 million	-2.5 pct</p>
